course: dictionary
lesson: 5705
title: Who is a Londoner?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Londoner is a person who lives in London, or who comes from there. London is the capital city of England and the United Kingdom, so many people in the country know a Londoner when they meet one.
explain: Read the clue words around the new word. «A born and bred Londoner» tells you that the person was born in London and grew up there. So a Londoner is someone whose home, and often whole life, is in London.
explain: When you see «Londoners» with an s, it means more than one person. «Londoners use the Tube» means lots of people from London travel on the Tube, which is London's underground train system.
fact: A Londoner is a person who lives in or comes from London.
fact: London is the capital city of England and the United Kingdom.
fact: «A born and bred Londoner» means someone who was born and raised in London.
fact: Londoners is the plural, which means more than one Londoner.
fact: In London talk, «bare» means very or lots, as in «It's bare cold», which means «It is very cold».
exercise: A Londoner is a person who lives in or comes from which city? | Paris | Edinburgh | *London | Manchester
exercise: In «Londoners use the Tube», which word names the people? | use | the | Tube | *Londoners
exercise: Ella was born in London and has lived there all her life. What is she? | A Geordie | A Scot | *A Londoner | An Australian
test: In «a Geordie says "howay, man"», what is a Geordie? | A Scot | A person from Bristol | *A person from the Newcastle area | A Londoner
test: Which city is the capital of England and the United Kingdom? | *London | Bristol | Newcastle | Glasgow
exam: Which phrase means someone who was born and raised in London? | *a born and bred Londoner | a dreich day | a servo | a gurt big hill
